course: dictionary
lesson: 5009
title: Words that spread
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Infectious means able to pass from one person or animal to another. Germs travel through the air, water, food or touch, so an infectious illness can spread. «Measles is one of the most infectious diseases known.»
explain: The word can also describe a feeling. An infectious laugh spreads quickly, and soon everyone in the room is laughing too. Read the clues: what happens to the other people?
explain: Look at the sentence around the word. «When you visit someone who is ill, wash your hands and keep your distance if they are infectious.» Keeping your distance tells you the illness could reach you, so infectious means it can be passed on.
fact: Infectious means able to be passed from one person or animal to another.
fact: Germs can spread through the air, water, food or touch.
fact: Handwashing, covering coughs and staying home when ill all stop germs spreading.
fact: Not every disease is infectious: diabetes and allergies cannot be passed on.
fact: An infectious laugh or smile spreads quickly to other people.
exercise: «When you visit someone who is ill, wash your hands and keep your distance if they are infectious.» What does infectious mean here? | Very tall | Covered in red spots | *Able to pass an illness to others | Feeling very sad
exercise: Which of these is NOT an infectious disease? | Flu | A stomach bug | *Diabetes | Chickenpox
exercise: «Jamal's giggle was so infectious that soon the whole class was giggling too.» What does infectious mean here? | Hidden under the desk | Dangerous to touch | Very quiet | *Spreading quickly to other people
test: «Measles is one of the most infectious diseases known.» What does most infectious mean? | Found only in the summer | *Easiest to catch from one person to another | Least dangerous of all | Hardest to pronounce
test: Which action stops germs spreading? | *Covering your cough and washing your hands | Going to school with a fever | Sharing your drink with friends | Sneezing into the air
exam: Which phrase best matches an infectious laugh? | A laugh that hurts your ears | *A laugh that spreads to other people | A cough that won't stop | A laugh that nobody can hear
